00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,680
In this video, we'll show you how to activate your BurpSuite Enterprise Edition license.

2
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:14,280
The first time you log in, you'll be prompted to activate your license key before you can

3
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:19,440
begin using the product. First of all, make sure that your Enterprise server can connect

4
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:25,920
to portswigger.net on port 443. If your server does not have direct access to the internet,

5
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:33,680
you may need to configure an HTTP proxy server, so have these details handy. Your BurpSuite license

6
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:40,000
covers a single deployment which can have multiple scanning machines and run multiple scans. If you

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,120
want to deploy the BurpSuite Enterprise server in multiple environments, for example you want to

8
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:51,120
have a separate Enterprise server and database for your test, development or staging environment,

9
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:57,280
then a separate license would be required. You can download your license key from the account

10
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:02,640
page of your Portswigger account. You then need to log into your Enterprise server and you'll be

11
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,880
prompted to upload your license.

12
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:20,640
If your license is activated successfully, the system displays a confirmation message

13
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:26,480
showing the details of the license key. If a connection to portswigger.net could not be established,

14
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:30,480
you will be prompted to configure an HTTP proxy before continuing.

